<section id=3D"A3.SS2" class=3D"ltx_subsection">
<h3 class=3D"ltx_title ltx_title_subsection">
<span class=3D"ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.2 </span>ANOVA results</h3>

<div id=3D"A3.SS2.p1" class=3D"ltx_para">
<p id=3D"A3.SS2.p1.1" class=3D"ltx_p">We apply ANOVA to analyze how factors=
 like requirement <span id=3D"A3.SS2.p1.1.1" class=3D"ltx_text ltx_font_ita=
lic">scope</span>, <span id=3D"A3.SS2.p1.1.2" class=3D"ltx_text ltx_font_it=
alic">source</span>, <span id=3D"A3.SS2.p1.1.3" class=3D"ltx_text ltx_font_=
italic">category</span>, or <span id=3D"A3.SS2.p1.1.4" class=3D"ltx_text lt=
x_font_italic">model</span> impact LLM+Prompts performance on specified vs.=
 unspecified requirements.
For factors that are significant, we use Tukey=E2=80=99s HSD test to identi=
fy which specific group means are significantly different from each other.
Results are reported in Table&nbsp;<a href=3D"https://arxiv.org/html/2505.1=
3360v3#A3.T4" title=3D"Table 4 =E2=80=A3 C.2 ANOVA results =E2=80=A3 Append=
ix C Additional experiment results =E2=80=A3 What Prompts Don=E2=80=99t Say=
: Understanding and Managing Underspecification in LLM Prompts" class=3D"lt=
x_ref"><span class=3D"ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>.</p>
</div>
