<div id=3D"A4.I1.i1.p1" class=3D"ltx_para">
<p id=3D"A4.I1.i1.p1.1" class=3D"ltx_p"><span id=3D"A4.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class=
=3D"ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">health-consulting</span>: Offer symptom g=
uidance, medical info, first-aid tips, and health advice.</p>
</div>
</li>
<li id=3D"A4.I1.i2" class=3D"ltx_item" style=3D"list-style-type:none;">
<span class=3D"ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">=E2=80=A2</span>=20
<div id=3D"A4.I1.i2.p1" class=3D"ltx_para">
<p id=3D"A4.I1.i2.p1.1" class=3D"ltx_p"><span id=3D"A4.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class=
=3D"ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">lesson-planning</span>: Generate a lesson=
 plan for the given user query.</p>
</div>
</li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id=3D"A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3" class=3D"ltx_para">
<p id=3D"A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3.1" class=3D"ltx_p">We used two existing dataset=
s to run the LLM+Prompts on:
HealthBench&nbsp;<cite class=3D"ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">Arora et&nbsp;=
al. (<a href=3D"https://arxiv.org/html/2505.13360v3#bib.bib4" title=3D"" cl=
ass=3D"ltx_ref">2025</a>)</cite> for health consulting,
and lesson_plan&nbsp;<cite class=3D"ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">Adeniyi (<=
a href=3D"https://arxiv.org/html/2505.13360v3#bib.bib1" title=3D"" class=3D=
"ltx_ref">2026</a>)</cite> for lesson planning.</p>
</div>
<div id=3D"A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4" class=3D"ltx_para">
<ul id=3D"A4.I2" class=3D"ltx_itemize">
<li id=3D"A4.I2.i1" class=3D"ltx_item" style=3D"list-style-type:none;">
<span class=3D"ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">=E2=80=A2</span>=20
<div id=3D"A4.I2.i1.p1" class=3D"ltx_para">
<p id=3D"A4.I2.i1.p1.1" class=3D"ltx_p">For HealthBench, we use <span id=3D=
"A4.I2.i1.p1.1.1" class=3D"ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">gpt-4.1-mini</span=
> to label if each query is a medical consulting request from a user. We fi=
lter out the ones that are not medical consulting and the ones that are not=
 in English. We then sample 200 examples from the dataset.</p>
</div>
</li>
<li id=3D"A4.I2.i2" class=3D"ltx_item" style=3D"list-style-type:none;">
<span class=3D"ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">=E2=80=A2</span>=20
<div id=3D"A4.I2.i2.p1" class=3D"ltx_para">
<p id=3D"A4.I2.i2.p1.1" class=3D"ltx_p">For lesson_plan, we drop duplicated=
 queries and then sample 200 examples from the dataset.</p>
</div>
</li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>
<section id=3D"A4.SS0.SSS0.Px2" class=3D"ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class=3D"ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Requirements.</h4>

<div id=3D"A4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1" class=3D"ltx_para">
<p id=3D"A4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class=3D"ltx_p">We followed the same procedu=
re to curate requirements as in Appendix&nbsp;<a href=3D"https://arxiv.org/=
html/2505.13360v3#A1.SS3" title=3D"A.3 Process of requirements curation =E2=
=80=A3 Appendix A Details on Experiments Setups =E2=80=A3 What Prompts Don=
=E2=80=99t Say: Understanding and Managing Underspecification in LLM Prompt=
s" class=3D"ltx_ref"><span class=3D"ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.3</span></a> an=
d shared them in Appendix&nbsp;<a href=3D"https://arxiv.org/html/2505.13360=
v3#A1.SS5" title=3D"A.5 Complete list of curated requirements =E2=80=A3 App=
endix A Details on Experiments Setups =E2=80=A3 What Prompts Don=E2=80=99t =
Say: Understanding and Managing Underspecification in LLM Prompts" class=3D=
"ltx_ref"><span class=3D"ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.5</span></a>.
We found existing prompts provided by Anthropic and GPTs<span id=3D"footnot=
e7" class=3D"ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class=3D"ltx_note_mark">7</su=
p><span class=3D"ltx_note_outer"><span class=3D"ltx_note_content"><sup clas=
s=3D"ltx_note_mark">7</sup><span class=3D"ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">7</span><a =
href=3D"https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/resources/prompt-library/lesson=
-planner" title=3D"" class=3D"ltx_ref ltx_url ltx_font_typewriter">https://=
platform.claude.com/docs/en/resources/prompt-library/lesson-planner</a>,
<br class=3D"ltx_break"><a href=3D"https://github.com/linexjlin/GPTs/blob/3=
adfb7b38423b64a995057483c1f9007ed5f4da5/prompts/MedicalDiagnosisAssistant.m=
d" title=3D"" class=3D"ltx_ref ltx_url ltx_font_typewriter">https://github.=
com/linexjlin/GPTs/blob/3adfb7b38423b64a995057483c1f9007ed5f4da5/prompts/Me=
dicalDiagnosisAssistant.md</a></span></span></span>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id=3D"A4.SS0.SSS0.Px3" class=3D"ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class=3D"ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Results.</h4>

<div id=3D"A4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1" class=3D"ltx_para">
<p id=3D"A4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class=3D"ltx_p">We observed very similar emp=
irical results in the additional tasks we studied, showing our main finding=
s can be readily generalized to different tasks and models:</p>
</div>
<div id=3D"A4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2" class=3D"ltx_para">
<ol id=3D"A4.I3" class=3D"ltx_enumerate">
<li id=3D"A4.I3.i1" class=3D"ltx_item" style=3D"list-style-type:none;">
<span class=3D"ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(1)</span>=20
<div id=3D"A4.I3.i1.p1" class=3D"ltx_para">
<p id=3D"A4.I3.i1.p1.1" class=3D"ltx_p">There is a performance gap between =
specified and unspecified requirements (83.6% vs. 59.5%); models are able t=
o guess unspecified requirements frequently (25.1%); format-related / globa=
l / developer-written requirements are easier to guess (cf. Section&nbsp;<a=
 href=3D"https://arxiv.org/html/2505.13360v3#S3.SS2" title=3D"3.2 LLMs are =
often able to guess unspecified requirements but lack stability =E2=80=A3 3=
 How do LLM+Prompts Behave when Underspecified? =E2=80=A3 What Prompts Don=
=E2=80=99t Say: Understanding and Managing Underspecification in LLM Prompt=
s" class=3D"ltx_ref"><span class=3D"ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.2</span></a>).<=
/p>
</div>
</li>
<li id=3D"A4.I3.i2" class=3D"ltx_item" style=3D"list-style-type:none;">
<span class=3D"ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(2)</span>=20
<div id=3D"A4.I3.i2.p1" class=3D"ltx_para">
<p id=3D"A4.I3.i2.p1.1" class=3D"ltx_p">Unspecified requirements are more l=
ikely to regress over model updates (4.3% vs. 2.3%) (cf. Section&nbsp;<a hr=
ef=3D"https://arxiv.org/html/2505.13360v3#S3.SS3" title=3D"3.3 LLMs are mor=
e likely to regress on unspecified requirements when updated =E2=80=A3 3 Ho=
w do LLM+Prompts Behave when Underspecified? =E2=80=A3 What Prompts Don=E2=
=80=99t Say: Understanding and Managing Underspecification in LLM Prompts" =
class=3D"ltx_ref"><span class=3D"ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.3</span></a>).</p>
</div>
</li>
<li id=3D"A4.I3.i3" class=3D"ltx_item" style=3D"list-style-type:none;">
<span class=3D"ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(3)</span>=20
<div id=3D"A4.I3.i3.p1" class=3D"ltx_para">
<p id=3D"A4.I3.i3.p1.1" class=3D"ltx_p">LLMs are struggling with more requi=
rements (dropping from 95.0% to 78.5% when we increase the number from 1 to=
 19) (cf. Section&nbsp;<a href=3D"https://arxiv.org/html/2505.13360v3#S3.SS=
4" title=3D"3.4 LLMs struggle with following many requirements at the same =
time =E2=80=A3 3 How do LLM+Prompts Behave when Underspecified? =E2=80=A3 W=
hat Prompts Don=E2=80=99t Say: Understanding and Managing Underspecificatio=
n in LLM Prompts" class=3D"ltx_ref"><span class=3D"ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.=
4</span></a>).</p>
</div>
</li>
<li id=3D"A4.I3.i4" class=3D"ltx_item" style=3D"list-style-type:none;">
<span class=3D"ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(4)</span>=20
<div id=3D"A4.I3.i4.p1" class=3D"ltx_para">
<p id=3D"A4.I3.i4.p1.1" class=3D"ltx_p">We also found the results hold for =
newer reasoning models we tested (<span id=3D"A4.I3.i4.p1.1.1" class=3D"ltx=
_text ltx_font_typewriter">gemini-2.5-flash</span>).</p>
</div>
</li>
</ol>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id=3D"A5" class=3D"ltx_appendix">
<h2 class=3D"ltx_title ltx_title_appendix">
<span class=3D"ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix E </span>Details on Agent=
ic Coding Case Study</h2>

<section id=3D"A5.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class=3D"ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class=3D"ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Prompt and requirements.</h4>

<div id=3D"A5.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class=3D"ltx_para">
<p id=3D"A5.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class=3D"ltx_p">We identified a system promp=
t for front-end development from Cursor Community.<span id=3D"footnote8" cl=
ass=3D"ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class=3D"ltx_note_mark">8</sup><spa=
n class=3D"ltx_note_outer"><span class=3D"ltx_note_content"><sup class=3D"l=
tx_note_mark">8</sup><span class=3D"ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">8</span><a href=
=3D"https://cursor.directory/gatsby-development-best-practices" title=3D"" =
class=3D"ltx_ref ltx_url ltx_font_typewriter">https://cursor.directory/gats=
by-development-best-practices</a></span></span></span>
The system prompt consists of a list of 25 requirements grouped by categori=
es (e.g., TypeScript Usage, UI and Styling).</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id=3D"A5.SS0.SSS0.Px2" class=3D"ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class=3D"ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Optimizers.</h4>

<div id=3D"A5.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1" class=3D"ltx_para">
<p id=3D"A5.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class=3D"ltx_p">We use the same optimizers w=
ith the same setup as in Section&nbsp;<a href=3D"https://arxiv.org/html/250=
5.13360v3#S4.SS2" title=3D"4.2 Designing requirement-aware prompt optimizer=
s =E2=80=A3 4 Requirements-Aware Prompt Optimization =E2=80=A3 What Prompts=
 Don=E2=80=99t Say: Understanding and Managing Underspecification in LLM Pr=
ompts" class=3D"ltx_ref"><span class=3D"ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.2</span></a=
>.
For the Bayesian optimizer, we split the prompt into different segments bas=
ed on the requirements, and the optimizer will choose the segments to inclu=
de in the final prompt.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id=3D"A5.SS0.SSS0.Px3" class=3D"ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class=3D"ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Evaluation.</h4>

<div id=3D"A5.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1" class=3D"ltx_para">
<p id=3D"A5.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class=3D"ltx_p">For a proposed prompt, we ru=
n it on each user query three times to reduce the variance of the generated=
 code repository.
Each run is executed with OpenHands scaffolds using <span id=3D"A5.SS0.SSS0=
.Px3.p1.1.1" class=3D"ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Qwen3-30B-A3B-Instruct-=
2507</span>, provided with TerminalTool, FileEditorTool, and TaskTrackerToo=
l.
The generated code repository will then be packed into one single file with=
 Repomix and provided to <span id=3D"A5.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.2" class=3D"ltx_t=
ext ltx_font_typewriter">gemini-2.5-flash</span> for evaluation.
The evaluator model has access to all 25 requirements and will evaluate the=
 code repository based on how well it adheres to the requirements, producin=
g an average accuracy across requirements.</p>
</div>
